-- title:
--   Galois-equivariant transport between two Néron objects at p
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $p^2 \nmid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, and a witness $hj$ that the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` of $j$ lies in the $q$-expansion function field of $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$; let $\mathfrak{X}$ be an integral model datum `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` for $X_H(M)$ over $R p = \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Given two level data $\Lambda, \Lambda'$ at $A$ and two Néron objects $O$ over $\Lambda$ and $O'$ over $\Lambda'$, assume for each of them that the designation consisting of the total space $O.G$, its structure morphism $O.g$ and the unit section of the relative group law represents the relative Picard functor of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$, cut out by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero ($hD$, $hD'$), and that the points dictionary $x \mapsto O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ (respectively $O'.\mathrm{pts}$) is additive for the multiplication of the group law obtained from that representability ($h_{\mathrm{pts,law}}$, $h_{\mathrm{pts,law}}'$); assume further that $\Lambda'.f$ is smooth and proper with connected fibres and carries a relative group law. Then there is an additive automorphism $e$ of $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot X_H(M)$ commuting with the action of every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, such that for every $m > 0$ the image under $e$ of $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$ (the subgroup generated by the toric points attached to the $\mu$-coordinate characters) is $O'.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, and the image under $e$ of $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$ (the subgroup generated by those $m$-torsion classes whose associated point extends to a section over $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$) is $O'.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$.
--
--   This is the uniqueness, up to a Galois-equivariant isomorphism respecting the toric and finite filtration pieces, of a Néron object for $J_H(M)$ at a place above $p$ satisfying the Picard-representability and points-additivity axioms. It feeds the comparison of toric and finite parts used in the level-lowering analysis at $p \parallel M$, and is invoked by the variant of the statement that dispenses with the points-law hypotheses.
-- source:
